Subject: [PATCH] spl: compile gzip decompressor with -O3
Upstream-Status: Pending

The V851S SPL spends most FIT load time outside NAND reads. Keep the
compression-sensitive zlib code at -O3 while the rest of SPL uses -Oz.
The standalone object preserves its optimization through the LTO link.

---
 lib/zlib/Makefile | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/zlib/Makefile b/lib/zlib/Makefile
--- a/lib/zlib/Makefile
+++ b/lib/zlib/Makefile
@@ -3,4 +3,8 @@
 # (C) Copyright 2000-2006
 # Wolfgang Denk, DENX Software Engineering, wd@denx.de.
 
+ifeq ($(CONFIG_SPL_BUILD),y)
+CFLAGS_zlib.o += -O3 -fno-lto
+endif
+
 obj-y += zlib.o
